    {
      "id": "18766",
      "key": "SFCC-417",
      "summary": "Global-e Cross-Border Integration — Custom Configuration & Order Sync",
      "description": "Epic Name:\n Global-e Cross-Border Integration — Custom Configuration & Order Sync\nEpic Summary\nThis epic covers the Zimmermann-specific configuration and custom code required to complete the Global-e cross-border checkout/order integration on top of the vendor-provided \nint_globale\n/\nint_globale_headless\n cartridges, across the 4 Global-e sites (ZimmermannUSIntl, ZimmermannEUIntl, ZimmermannHK, ZimmermannME). It follows a gap analysis comparing Global-e's official SFCC Integration Guide and OCAPI/SCAPI Support guide against the current repo state — see \ndocs/Global-e/main-config-gap-analysis.md\n and \ndocs/Global-e/ocapi-scapi-gap-analysis.md\n in the zimmermann-sfcc repo.\nBusiness Value / Objective\nGlobal-e sites cannot reliably go live for cross-border customers until these gaps are closed: scheduled Global-e jobs are currently misconfigured against the vendor's demo site rather than Zimmermann's real sites, the payment-redirect flow for Global-e's hosted checkout is unbuilt (a checkout-breaking gap since Global-e is a hosted payment page for this project), and SCAPI integration settings are incomplete. Completing this epic is a precondition for Global-e site launch readiness.\nScope\nIn Scope:\nFixing the Global-e scheduled job site-assignment misconfiguration\nCompleting non-secret Global-e SCAPI site preference configuration\nBuilding the headless payment-redirect endpoint (SCAPI)\nSFCC OMS order-status sync decision + implementation (conditional on OMS usage)\nOutbound Global-e order-notification hook wiring (dispatch/refund/RMA sync trigger)\nSFCC order shipping-status update on dispatch to the Global-e hub\nOCAPI/SCAPI resource-permission deployment for the 4 Global-e sites\nEnvironment/BM configuration checklist (feature switch, payment processor, order preferences allow-list, mandatory merchant-connection identifiers)\nDecision on optional Global-e custom hook extension points (marketing consent, cookie consent)\nOut of Scope:\nVendor cartridge internals (\nint_globale\n/\nint_globale_headless\n) — not modified, only extended via documented hook points\nThe Price Book pricing strategy business decision itself (Dynamic/Fixed/Shared per country) — tracked as a dependency/blocker, not a deliverable of this epic\nPWA/storefront-side implementation (checkout iframe, SDK init, cookie persistence) — owned by the PWA workspace; only the SFCC-side endpoint is in scope here\nGlobal-e analytics / OnCheckoutStepLoaded integration — separate doc not yet reviewed, will be a follow-up epic once reviewed\nConfig drift-detection tooling — cross-cutting concern tracked separately in \ndocs/config-drift-detection-design.md\n, not Global-e-specific\nTriggering MuleSoft's Magento Experience API on order creation — covered by the Adyen epic (SFCC-659, story SFCC-671), since the same SCAPI order-creation hook fires for both Adyen-approved domestic orders and Global-e-confirmed international orders; not duplicated here\nDependencies\nGlobal-e onboarding must supply the 4 mandatory merchant-connection identifiers (Merchant GUID, Client JS Merchant ID, API URL, Client JS SDK Base URL — \ngeMerchantGuid\n/\ngeClientJsMerchantId\n/\ngeApiUrl\n/\ngeClientJsBaseUrl\n) from the Global-e Project/Account Manager, plus the SCAPI settings values (Organization ID, Short Code, Version, Redirect URI, Auth Type, Client ID/Secret)\nBusiness decision on Price Book pricing strategy (Dynamic/Fixed/Shared) per country — blocks storefront/promotion validation\nDecision on whether Zimmermann uses SFCC OMS for Global-e order fulfillment — blocks the order-status sync story\nReal SCAPI client ID needed before OCAPI JSON permissions can be deployed to any site\nPWA team's cookie-persistence implementation for the payment-redirect flow\nSFCC-671 (Adyen epic) fires MuleSoft's Magento Experience API on order creation, including for Global-e-confirmed international orders — coordinate with that story to confirm no overlap with this epic's outbound order-notification story (dispatch/refund/RMA)\nAssumptions & Constraints\nThis project is SCAPI-only, pure headless (no SFRA/SiteGenesis templates) — confirmed via cartridge path audit\nAll 4 Global-e sites (USIntl, EUIntl, HK, ME) share identical custom-code requirements; only configuration values differ per site\nGlobal-e is confirmed to be a hosted payment page for this project — the payment-redirect handling is mandatory, not optional",
      "status": {
        "name": "To Do",
        "category": "To Do",
        "color": "blue-gray"
