    {
      "id": "13711",
      "body": "User:557058:1a7fb05a-783b-4241-a0f1-9a7b046da3a8 Here are some options:\nTSD §5.3 = [Technical Solution Design PWA](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/256835585/TechnicalSolutionDesignPWA)\nOption A — PWA Kit config module (aligned with TSD §5.3) ✅ Recommended\nThe country-to-site mapping from the Confluence table lives in a typed TypeScript module in the PWA Kit repo (e.g. app/config/countries.ts). This module is the single source of truth for:\nCountry → regional site assignment (routing)\nAddress form country options per storefront\nGlobal-e flag determination (international vs. domestic checkout owner)\nShipping country selector population\nPros:\nDirectly aligned with TSD §5.3 — no architectural deviation\nType-safe, testable, version-controlled alongside the PWA\nZero latency (no API call), works at SSR time without an SCAPI round-trip\nAdding a market triggers a PWA deploy anyway (new locale URLs, routing rules, SFCC site config) — the country list change isn't an isolated admin operation\nCons:\nA Site Admin cannot change it without a code deploy — but this is by design given how tightly the list is coupled to routing logic, locales, and SFCC site setup\nThe story's framing (\"Site Admin configures the list\") needs refinement in the AC\nImplementation note: the overrides/ directory pattern the project uses means this config module sits under overrides/app/config/countries.ts, following the template extensibility model.\nOption B — SFCC Custom Objects  custom SCAPI endpoint\nStore the mapping in a BM-managed Custom Object, expose via a custom endpoint in plugin\\*zim\\*scapi, fetch at runtime from the PWA.\nPros: Admin-editable without a code deploy.\nCons:\nContradicts TSD §5.3 directly\nAdds an SCAPI call on every page that needs the list (or requires a caching layer)\nCountry changes still require SFCC site creation, locale config, PWA routing rules, and a PWA deploy — so the \"admin self-service\" benefit is illusory for the real-world workflow\nCreates two sources of truth (BM object + PWA routing config)\nData would still need to be bootstrapped via the data/core/ Site Archive import pipeline\nNot recommended unless there is a confirmed requirement for admin-only runtime changes to the country list that don't touch any other layer.\nOption C — Contentful\nManage as a structured content type in Contentful, fetch via CDA.\nCons: Contentful is for editorial/CMS content. Routing config is infrastructure, not content. The integration is also not yet stable (SFCC-249 TSD still in progress). Adds unnecessary dependency to a critical routing path.",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Victor T. Crisostomo",
        "name": "Victor T. Crisostomo",
        "email": "victor.t.crisostomo@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:09af9e5b-661b-42a2-90ec-9ce9f69d324d/0ead87b0-7d31-4296-b27b-4a7b26ac2af1/48"
      },
