{"result":"{
  "id": "18661",
  "key": "SFCC-327",
  "summary": "Checkout – Guest Sign-In Block (Email Input & Send Code Button)",
  "description": "As a Shopper, I want to enter my email address and request a one-time sign-in code at checkout, so that I can authenticate without needing a password.\n\nThis component appears on the checkout entry page for unauthenticated users (Image 1), above the delivery address section. It comprises two elements: an email address text input field and a \"Send Code\" CTA button below it. It does not include social sign-in buttons (see SFCC-346 for Apple and Google sign-in). The component is hidden once the user is authenticated. Surface: PWA Kit / SFCC checkout page. Owned by: SFCC/PWA Kit. Depends on CFD-001, CFD-007, CFD-013. Cross-epic dependency: My Account authentication epic.",
  "status": {
    "name": "To Do",
    "category": "To Do",
    "color": "blue-gray"
  },
  "comments": [
    {
      "id": "13689",
      "body": "## Passwordless Login — Implementation Gap Analysis\n\nThe following gaps have been identified for the OTP passwordless login implementation on PWA Kit / MRT. This covers backend configuration, integration, codebase, and open decisions.\n\n----\n\n### ✅ Already Done\n\n- SLAS private client configured\n- `sfcc.pwdless_login` scope assigned\n- MRT environment variables for SLAS (`SLAS_CLIENT_ID`, `SLAS_CLIENT_SECRET`) confirmed set across environments\n\n----\n\n### SLAS Configuration\n\n- Callback URL not yet registered in SLAS Admin UI — needs to be added once the MRT callback endpoint is built and deployed\n- OTP token length not decided or configured (default is 8 digits; 6-digit option available in SLAS Admin UI)\n\n----\n\n### Email Delivery\n\n  - **No Agentforce Marketing license on this project* — native SLAS email mode is blocked\n  - Project email stack is **Emarsys* (confirmed via Confluence: 1.4 Third Party Overview)\n- Callback mode is the required path — needs an MRT callback endpoint that dispatches OTP via Emarsys transactional API\n- Emarsys transactional API capability for OTP dispatch not yet confirmed with the Emarsys integration owner\n- DMARC policy not yet checked for the sender domain\n\n----\n\n### MRT Environment Variables\n\n- `OTP_TOKEN_LENGTH` not set (must match SLAS Admin UI setting once decided)\n- `PASSWORDLESS_CALLBACK_URI` not set (blocked until callback endpoint is built and deployed)\n\n----\n\n### PWA Kit Codebase\n\n- Retail React App version not confirmed as 6.0+ (required minimum for passwordless login)\n- Passwordless login disabled by default — `enabled: false` in `config/default.js` needs to be flipped\n- `mode` must be set to `'callback'` in config\n- MRT callback endpoint route needs to be built to receive the SLAS POST and dispatch OTP via Emarsys\n- Decision needed: is new shopper registration via OTP in scope? (requires `register_customer=true` on the `authorizePasswordlessCustomer` API call)\n\n----\n\n### Integration / Architecture\n\n  - **Omneo sync risk:* behaviour of SLAS-created customer profiles against the existing Omneo ↔ SFCC sync is unconfirmed — potential for orphaned customer records outside Omneo\n- Per-environment SLAS client strategy not decided: single client with one callback URL vs separate clients per environment (dev/staging/prod)\n\n----\n\n### Open Decisions\n\n|Decision|Options|\n|---|---|\n|OTP token length|6 or 8 digits|\n|New registration via OTP|In scope or out of scope|\n|OTP delivery channel|Emarsys email vs Amazon SNS (SMS)|\n|SLAS client per environment|Single client vs separate per environment|\n\n----\n\n*Gap analysis based on Confluence (1.4 Third Party Overview, 04.3.1 BM User Roles & Permissions Matrix) and SLAS/PWA Kit documentation.*",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Victor T. Crisostomo",
        "name": "Victor T. Crisostomo",
        "email": "victor.t.crisostomo@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:09af9e5b-661b-42a2-90ec-9ce9f69d324d/0ead87b0-7d31-4296-b27b-4a7b26ac2af1/48"
      },
      "created": "2026-08-05T17:02:05.421+1000",
      "updated": "2026-08-05T17:02:05.421+1000"
