    {
      "id": "13812",
      "body": "User:712020:c99d37b3-9c93-4347-951d-5ffb32ff1341 Yes, we will cover the behaviour of the product card component also in each page (please note some of these are still draft stories):\n[SFCC-185 PLP UI – Quick Add to Bag - Jira](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-185)\n[SFCC-497 Wishlist – Add to Bag Icon / CTA - Jira](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-497)\n[SFCC-84](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-84) \n[SFCC-90 Homepage Layout & Content Modules UI - Jira](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-90)\n\nI will link all of these as related tickets.",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "email": "jasmijn.tsang@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d/40fcd533-06f6-4e5b-ba9f-23879e1193f9/48"
      },
      "created": "2026-08-12T09:39:18.300+1000",
      "updated": "2026-08-12T09:39:18.300+1000"
    }
  ],
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "*Core component*\n\n# Given a product is passed to the card component, when it renders, then the primary product image and product name are always displayed regardless of variation.\n# Given a product has a badge (e.g. Runway), when the card renders in any variation, then the badge is displayed in the correct position per Figma.\n# Given the component is built as a PWA component, when imported into any page surface, then it renders correctly without page-specific logic embedded in the component itself.\n# Given the card renders, when on desktop and the user hovers{color:#ff5630}, {color}then the tile image switches from the item/flat photo to the model photo.\n\n*PLP variation*\n\n# Given the card renders on PLP, when it is in the default state, then the image, name, badge, price (incl. was/now), and cart icon are visible.\n# Given the card renders on PLP, when on desktop and the user hovers, then the size selector becomes visible and the price disappears.\n# Given the card renders on PLP, when on desktop and the user hovers, then the arrows appear for the shopper to click through the product images.\n# Given the card renders on PLP, when on mobile, then the size selector is not displayed.\n# Given a product is out of stock, when the card renders, then the cart is greyed out and a notify me link appears on hover instead of price.\n\n*Home page variation*\n\n# Given the card renders on home page, when it is in the default state, then the image, name, and badge are displayed.\n# Given the card renders on home page, when on desktop and the user hovers, then the arrows appear for the shopper to click through the product images.\n# Given the card renders on home page, when on desktop and the user hovers, then the price (incl. was/now) appears.\n# Given the card renders on home page, when on mobile, then the user only sees the image and name.\n\n*Wishlist variation*\n\n# Given the card renders on the wishlist, when it is in the default state, then the image, cart icon, name, colour, size, badge, and price (incl. was/now) are displayed.\n# Given the card renders on the wishlist, then there is a remove ('x') cta on the top right.\n\n*Recently Viewed Full History variation (same behavior as PLP card)*\n\n# Given the card renders on the View Full History Page, when it is in the default state, then the image, name, badge, price (incl. was/now), and cart icon are visible.\n# Given the card renders on PLP, when on desktop and the user hovers, then the size selector becomes visible and the price disappears.\n# Given the card renders on PLP, when on desktop and the user hovers, then the arrows appear for the shopper to click through the product images.\n# Given the card renders on PLP, when on mobile, then the size selector is not displayed.\n# Given a product is out of stock, when the card renders, then the cart is greyed out and a notify me link appears on hover instead of price.\n\n*Variation extensibility*\n\n# Given a new style is introduced in future (e.g. Search), when added to the component, then it can be configured without restructuring the base component."
  }
}"}

